WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.602
-A Senate report provides

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:05.137
damning new details
about Donald Trump's attempts

00:00:05.137 --> 00:00:07.473
to get the Justice Department
to overturn the election

00:00:07.473 --> 00:00:08.775
and, yet, former Trump allies

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:10.477
who criticized him
for the attempted coup,

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:11.877
like Nikki Haley and Mike Pence,

00:00:11.877 --> 00:00:13.112
are pathetically
falling back in line.

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:15.381
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:19.485
♪♪

00:00:19.485 --> 00:00:21.654
If you recall -- and I know
it's hard to remember,

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:24.023
since it happened approximately
78 years ago --

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:26.492
Donald Trump whipped up
a violent mob

00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:28.794
to attack the Capitol
and stage an insurrection,

00:00:28.794 --> 00:00:31.730
in order to overturn the results
of a free and fair election.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:33.999
I'm no lawyer, but that, alone,

00:00:33.999 --> 00:00:36.002
seems to me like a crime worthy
of jail time.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.437
And by the way,
when I say I'm not a lawyer,

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:39.171
that doesn't mean
I don't know lawyers.

00:00:39.171 --> 00:00:41.807
I feel like everyone
I know is a lawyer.

00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:43.810
The other day, I was
at the dentist's office,

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.145
getting a cleaning, and, when I
mentioned a parking ticket,

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:48.915
my hygienist said,
"Do you need representation?"

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:50.016
and gave me his card.
Although,

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:51.918
I should be clear,
my dental hygienist

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:53.619
is Rudy Giuliani.

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:55.554
I'm sorry.
He's just cheaper.

00:00:55.554 --> 00:00:58.090
I think it's because he uses
helium, instead of nitrous.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:00:59.558
I say that because it always
hurts a ton

00:00:59.558 --> 00:01:01.560
and, when I scream in pain,
it sounds like this --

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.563
[ Donald Duck voice ]
No! Dad, no!

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:07.199
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.199 --> 00:01:09.001
Alright.

00:01:09.001 --> 00:01:10.202
And, yet, it seems like,

00:01:10.202 --> 00:01:12.204
not only is Trump likely
to avoid jail,

00:01:12.204 --> 00:01:14.074
but, according to a report
from earlier this week,

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:16.142
he wants to run
for president again.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.710 line:0%
-New reporting on Donald Trump's

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.579 line:0%
future presidential ambitions.

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:21.914 line:0%
Three sources tell
The Washington Post

00:01:21.914 --> 00:01:24.317 line:0%
that Trump asked advisors
whether he should announce

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:26.486 line:0%
his 2024 bid for the White House

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:29.322 line:0%
after the chaotic exit
in Afghanistan

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:32.792 line:0%
and those advisors
urged "patience."

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.393 line:0%
That's the quote, patience.

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:35.995 line:0%
But, behind the scenes,
there's concern

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:39.899 line:0%
that Democrats could benefit
during the 2022 midterms,

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:42.001 line:0%
if Trump decides to jump

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.537 line:0%
into the presidential race
before that.

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:46.773
-It says a lot
about how unpopular Trump is,

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.741
that his advisors had
to tell him to wait

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:51.076
to announce his candidacy,
or it would help Democrats.

00:01:51.076 --> 00:01:53.846
But would anyone really be
shocked if he ran again?

00:01:53.846 --> 00:01:56.416
He tried everything,
in and out of his power,

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:58.217
to stay in the White House,
even though he lost.

00:01:58.217 --> 00:01:59.818
He begged the Georgia
secretary of state

00:01:59.818 --> 00:02:02.722
to find some votes, like he was
Jack Lemmon in a phone booth.

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:04.223
Assuming he's not going
to run again

00:02:04.223 --> 00:02:06.425
is like hitting Michael Myers
with a car

00:02:06.425 --> 00:02:07.660
and thinking the movie's over.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.394
"Oh, he fell down.

00:02:09.394 --> 00:02:10.897
Okay, we're all safe now.

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:12.765
We can turn our backs on him."

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:15.000
Trump probably understands
the place he'd be safest

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.803
from his current legal troubles
is the White House,

00:02:17.803 --> 00:02:19.906
so, it makes sense he'd want
to get back there.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:22.341
He treats the job less like
a massive responsibility

00:02:22.341 --> 00:02:26.211
and more like a safe base
in a game of middle school tag.

00:02:26.211 --> 00:02:27.280
[ As Trump ]
I'm touching the
Oval Office wall.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.448
I'm safe when
I'm touching the wall.

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:30.583
You can't arrest me.
I'm touching the wall.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.218
So Trump is reportedly
considering running again

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:34.353
and other aspiring Republicans
have said

00:02:34.353 --> 00:02:35.822
they'll wait
until he makes the decision

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.490
before they decide
to run themselves.

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:39.325 line:0%
-Former UN Ambassador
Nikki Haley

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:42.729 line:0%
now says the Republican Party
needs former President Trump

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:43.963 line:0%
and she'll consult with him,

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:46.332 line:0%
if she makes a bid
for the White House.

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:48.801 line:0%
-She called Donald Trump
a friend

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.570 line:0%
and said she would consult
with him

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:53.139 line:0%
before launching a run
for the White House.

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:55.574 line:0%
-"We need him
in the Republican Party.

00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:59.912 line:0%
I don't want us to go back
to the days before Trump."

00:02:59.912 --> 00:03:01.080
-You don't?!

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.148
What was wrong
with the days before Trump,

00:03:03.148 --> 00:03:04.918
too many alive people?

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:06.419
Not enough breaking news alerts?

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:08.587
There was so much insanity
during Trump

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:09.922
that the breaking news banner

00:03:09.922 --> 00:03:12.759
was seared into my flatscreen
even when it was off.

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:14.894
But that tells you
everything right there.

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:16.395
They want the Trump years
back again.

00:03:16.395 --> 00:03:18.597
That's what happens when you're
a boring, soulless hack

00:03:18.597 --> 00:03:21.167
who's dedicated your life
to pursuing power above all else

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:23.102
in a place like
official Washington,

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.169
where everyone around you is

00:03:24.169 --> 00:03:25.471
a balding weirdo
with no interests,

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.973
aside from raising money
and running for things,

00:03:27.973 --> 00:03:31.277
or maybe writing one of these
airport terminal dust catchers.

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:33.846
The Nikki Haleys of the world
used to spend their time

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:35.714
at boring
think tank cocktail parties

00:03:35.714 --> 00:03:37.383
where the hot topic was
who's getting invited

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:40.085
to the Heritage Foundation
Christmas party, then, suddenly,

00:03:40.085 --> 00:03:42.921
an amoral reality show psycho
like Trump comes along

00:03:42.921 --> 00:03:45.958
and uses dirty words and they
think they're in Hollywood now.

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:47.326
It's like when you go
to Times Square

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:49.095
for the first time
and think you're meeting

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:50.463
the real Iron Man.

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.631
"He said he was going to use
his jet boots to fly away,

00:03:52.631 --> 00:03:56.135
but then, I saw him smoking
a cigarette on the F train."

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.337
[ Laughter ]
That's what happened
to Lindsey Graham.

00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:58.637
He started out hating Trump,

00:03:58.637 --> 00:04:00.839
like Trump was a slick
out-of-towner dating his meemaw,

00:04:00.839 --> 00:04:03.175
but then, Graham realized
he could be in show business,

00:04:03.175 --> 00:04:04.244
and everything changed.

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:05.978
[ As Graham ]
Meemaw, Mr. Trump says

00:04:05.978 --> 00:04:07.746
he's going to get me a job
in the pictures.

00:04:07.746 --> 00:04:10.049
I just need to give him $200
for new headshots.

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:12.752
What do you mean,
how am I going to get $200?!

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:14.721
We're going to sell the farm,
you old coot!

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:15.921
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.921 --> 00:04:17.924
That's why Nikki Haley wants
Trump days back

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:20.526
and why she suddenly considers
Trump her friend again,

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:22.494
after telling Politico,
earlier this year,

00:04:22.494 --> 00:04:24.998
that he was no longer welcome
in national politics.

00:04:39.945 --> 00:04:41.346
Let's be honest -- these people

00:04:41.346 --> 00:04:42.948
were always going
to forgive him.

00:04:42.948 --> 00:04:44.617
Republicans are like
the rich housewife

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:46.518
who finds lipstick
on her husband's collar

00:04:46.518 --> 00:04:47.920
and tells her friend,
"He says he got it

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.756
because he slipped and fell
into a makeup counter.

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:52.992
And you know the floor
of Bloomingdale's

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:54.927
is like an ice skating rink."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:56.862
So the Nikki Haleys
and Lindsey Grahams of the world

00:04:56.862 --> 00:04:58.830
briefly distance themselves
from Trump

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:00.199
and then quickly fell back
in line,

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:01.633
despite the fact
that he repeatedly tried

00:05:01.633 --> 00:05:03.736
to overturn the results
of a free and fair election

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:05.237
and destroy our democracy.

00:05:05.237 --> 00:05:07.440
And it isn't like January 6th

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.675
with just some protest
that got out of hand

00:05:09.675 --> 00:05:12.545
after an impulsive Trump
vented his frustrations.

00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:15.047
They had a plan. In fact,
they had multiple plans.

00:05:15.047 --> 00:05:17.015 line:0%
As we've explained before,
one of Trump's lawyers,

00:05:17.015 --> 00:05:18.484 line:0%
a guy named John Eastman,

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:20.686 line:0%
even wrote an instruction manual
for Mike Pence,

00:05:20.686 --> 00:05:22.421
laying out exactly how

00:05:22.421 --> 00:05:24.089
to overturn
the election results,

00:05:24.089 --> 00:05:26.859
which he did not have
the power to do.

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:29.228
Trump even brought them together
in the Oval Office

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:31.597
to try to convince Pence
to go through with it.

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:33.966 line:0%
-Stunning new details
on Donald Trump's efforts

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:36.001 line:0%
to overturn the 2020 election

00:05:36.001 --> 00:05:37.202 line:0%
from the new book "Peril,"

00:05:37.202 --> 00:05:39.138 line:0%
by Bob Woodward
and Robert Costa.

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:43.175 line:0%
The authors report on a two-page
memo drafted by John Eastman.

00:05:43.175 --> 00:05:45.077 line:0%
John Eastman
is a conservative lawyer

00:05:45.077 --> 00:05:47.713 line:0%
who was working
for Trump's legal team.

00:05:47.713 --> 00:05:50.016 line:0%
It amounts to a blueprint
for a coup.

00:05:50.016 --> 00:05:52.285 line:0%
NBC News has later
obtained the memo.

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:55.755 line:0%
It outlines how Pence was
to have disrupted

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:58.090 line:0%
the certification of the
Electoral College results

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:00.059 line:0%
and handed the election
to Trump.

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:03.396 line:0%
Trump tells Pence this
about Eastman --

00:06:09.502 --> 00:06:12.538
-But even weirder are
the juvenile tactics Trump used

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:15.208
to try to persuade Pence
to go through with it.

00:06:30.556 --> 00:06:32.291
The following day,
on the morning of January 6th,

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:34.227
he reportedly called Pence
and taunted...

00:06:38.930 --> 00:06:41.300
So he uses the same tactics
as a 14-year-old trying

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.834
to convince his friend
to steal a KitKat

00:06:42.834 --> 00:06:43.870
from a convenience store.

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:45.538
"Just hide it under your shirt."

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:46.772
I can't do that.

00:06:46.772 --> 00:06:48.106
"But wouldn't it be like cool,

00:06:48.106 --> 00:06:49.809
if you did?
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.809 --> 00:06:53.379
I don't know if I can be friends
with a wimp, Mike."

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:56.549
Also, I love that Trump was the
most powerful man in the world,

00:06:56.549 --> 00:06:59.618
with virtually unlimited
resources at his fingertips,

00:06:59.618 --> 00:07:01.487
and, yet, he thought
his biggest leverage

00:07:01.487 --> 00:07:04.556
was threatening not to be
Mike Pence's friend anymore.

00:07:04.556 --> 00:07:06.859
You're a terrible friend.

00:07:06.859 --> 00:07:08.160
I doubt Mike Pence was thinking,

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:10.629
"Oh, no, now who's going
to help me with my sofa

00:07:10.629 --> 00:07:12.198
next time I have to move?"

00:07:12.198 --> 00:07:13.632
Also, we know about all this.

00:07:13.632 --> 00:07:15.401
Can you imagine
what we don't know about?

00:07:15.401 --> 00:07:16.935
So far,
Bob Woodward's Trump books

00:07:16.935 --> 00:07:19.071
have been called "Fear,"
"Rage," and "Peril,"

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:20.807
but, at this rate, he's going
to have to call the next one...

00:07:22.775 --> 00:07:23.909 line:0%
Yet, Pence is now doing

00:07:23.909 --> 00:07:25.411 line:0%
the same song and dance
as Nikki Haley,

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:28.047 line:0%
and acting like that whole
mob riot thing was no big deal.

00:07:28.047 --> 00:07:30.416 line:0%
-The president and I sat down
a few days later

00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:31.884 line:0%
and talked through all of it.

00:07:31.884 --> 00:07:33.753 line:0%
I can tell you that we
parted amicably

00:07:33.753 --> 00:07:35.621 line:0%
at the end of the administration

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:37.556 line:0%
and we've talked
a number of times

00:07:37.556 --> 00:07:39.058 line:0%
since we both left office.

00:07:39.058 --> 00:07:43.095 line:0%
But, I believe
that our entire focus today

00:07:43.095 --> 00:07:44.430 line:0%
should be on the future.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:46.198 line:0%
I know the media wants
to distract

00:07:46.198 --> 00:07:48.200 line:0%
from the Biden administration's
failed agenda

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:50.969 line:0%
by focusing on one day
in January.

00:07:50.969 --> 00:07:52.838
-"One day in January"?

00:07:52.838 --> 00:07:55.140
If there was a day where
a violent mob was chanting,

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:57.476
"Hang Seth Meyers," I wouldn't
call it "one day in January."

00:07:57.476 --> 00:08:00.379
I'd call it "the day I moved
to Portugal and grew a beard."

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:01.747
[ Laughter ]
"One day in January"

00:08:01.747 --> 00:08:03.950 line:0%
sounds like a sports movie
starring Al Pacino

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:06.051 line:0%
as a past-his-prime
football coach.

00:08:06.051 --> 00:08:07.085 line:0%
[ As Pacino ]
Boom! Alright!

00:08:07.085 --> 00:08:09.087
[ Laughter ]
Let's pick a play.

00:08:09.087 --> 00:08:10.422
We got a passing play.

00:08:10.422 --> 00:08:11.490
We got running plays.

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:12.925
How about this --

00:08:12.925 --> 00:08:15.528
we just hang
the opposing quarterback.

00:08:15.528 --> 00:08:19.031
[ Laughter ]
That's hard-nosed
football, muchacho.

00:08:19.031 --> 00:08:21.600
[ Laughter ]

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.970
Last day to do my Pacino.

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:26.072
Oh, I meant last day
to do my Pacino

00:08:26.072 --> 00:08:27.473
without a standing ovation.

00:08:27.473 --> 00:08:30.809
[ Laughter ]

00:08:30.809 --> 00:08:33.045
And that wasn't the only
Oval Office meeting

00:08:33.045 --> 00:08:35.214
where Trump tried to pressure
a senior government official

00:08:35.214 --> 00:08:36.382
to help him overthrow democracy.

00:08:36.382 --> 00:08:37.749
We also know that one
of his henchmen

00:08:37.749 --> 00:08:40.352
in the Justice Department,
a guy named Jeffrey Clark,

00:08:40.352 --> 00:08:42.588
had a detailed plan for getting
the Justice Department

00:08:42.588 --> 00:08:44.090
to interfere and declare

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:45.958
there was fraud in the election,
which there was not.

00:08:45.958 --> 00:08:47.460
And, now, thanks to a new report

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:48.828
from the
Senate Judiciary Committee,

00:08:48.828 --> 00:08:51.764
we have more details about that
plan and that meeting.

00:08:51.764 --> 00:08:53.799 line:0%
-After an eight-month
investigation,

00:08:53.799 --> 00:08:57.536 line:0%
the Senate Judiciary Committee
today will release a report

00:08:57.536 --> 00:08:59.104 line:0%
on how the Trump administration

00:08:59.104 --> 00:09:01.039 line:0%
attempted to subvert the law,

00:09:01.039 --> 00:09:03.308 line:0%
in an effort to keep
the president in office.

00:09:03.308 --> 00:09:06.111 line:0%
The report provides new details
on the efforts

00:09:06.111 --> 00:09:09.715 line:0%
of then-Acting Assistant
Attorney General Jeffrey Clark,

00:09:09.715 --> 00:09:12.952 line:0%
as he attempted to do
the bidding of President Trump.

00:09:12.952 --> 00:09:15.020 line:0%
-The president
of the United States decided

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:16.789 line:0%
to put full court pressure

00:09:16.789 --> 00:09:19.658 line:0%
on the new acting attorney
general, Jeffrey Rosen.

00:09:19.658 --> 00:09:22.094 line:0%
And, as I said before,
he was relentless.

00:09:22.094 --> 00:09:23.896 line:0%
When you look
at the number of contacts --

00:09:23.896 --> 00:09:26.131 line:0%
we're still waiting
for even more evidence

00:09:26.131 --> 00:09:28.367 line:0%
to come in on that subject --

00:09:28.367 --> 00:09:31.136 line:0%
he was really pushing
the Department of Justice

00:09:31.136 --> 00:09:34.573 line:0%
to bend to his political will
and I will tell you,

00:09:34.573 --> 00:09:36.975 line:0%
just, I don't think
I'm overstating the case.

00:09:36.975 --> 00:09:38.244 line:0%
We were a half step away

00:09:38.244 --> 00:09:41.079 line:0%
from a full-blown
constitutional crisis.

00:09:41.079 --> 00:09:43.015
-Now, of course, half a step
is still a lot for Trump,

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:44.850
given how he takes steps.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:46.452
I've never seen a person
as confident as him

00:09:46.452 --> 00:09:47.920
walk as gingerly as he does.

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:50.589
He walks down a ramp
like a deer on a frozen pond.

00:09:50.589 --> 00:09:51.857
If you couldn't see his shoes,
you'd think

00:09:51.857 --> 00:09:54.193 line:0%
he was wearing roller skates
for the first time.

00:09:54.193 --> 00:09:55.327
But that's how close we came.

00:09:55.327 --> 00:09:56.962
Trump tried every avenue
he could think of --

00:09:56.962 --> 00:09:58.397
the courts, the states,
the vice president,

00:09:58.397 --> 00:09:59.565
the Justice Department.
He's like the guy

00:09:59.565 --> 00:10:01.500
in gridlock traffic
who keeps switching lanes

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:03.468
and then throws his hands up
when it doesn't work.

00:10:03.468 --> 00:10:05.204
We're on the FDR
at 5:00 in the afternoon.

00:10:05.204 --> 00:10:07.039
There's no secret way out,
buddy.

00:10:07.039 --> 00:10:08.940
In the end, the only thing
that stopped Trump, apparently,

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:12.011
was a threat from senior
DOJ officials to resign.

00:10:12.011 --> 00:10:13.212
As The New York Times
reported yesterday,

00:10:13.212 --> 00:10:15.014
just days
before the insurrection,

00:10:15.014 --> 00:10:16.415
Trump held a meeting
in the Oval Office

00:10:16.415 --> 00:10:17.717
about his plans for a coup.

00:10:44.944 --> 00:10:46.578
Pretty dramatic language.
Woodward's going to have

00:10:46.578 --> 00:10:49.915 line:0%
to up the ante on the next book
even more than I thought.

00:10:49.915 --> 00:10:51.283 line:0%
Although,
"murder-suicide pact" probably

00:10:51.283 --> 00:10:52.784 line:0%
sounded good to Trump
when he first heard it.

00:10:52.784 --> 00:10:54.986
[ As Trump ]
So I murder you and then,
you commit suicide?

00:10:54.986 --> 00:10:56.221
[ Laughter ]
I think I --

00:10:56.221 --> 00:10:58.390
I think I saw something
like that once on "SVU."

00:10:58.390 --> 00:11:00.392
[ Laughter ]
"SVU."

00:11:00.392 --> 00:11:02.061
We love "SVU," don't we, folks?

00:11:02.061 --> 00:11:03.929
A great,
a great American program.

00:11:03.929 --> 00:11:05.631
We love Mr. Ice-Lemonade

00:11:05.631 --> 00:11:07.866
and Richard Seltzer.

00:11:07.866 --> 00:11:09.267
[ Laughter ]
A real original.

00:11:09.267 --> 00:11:11.170
Detective John Munch!

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:12.638
[ Laughter ]

00:11:12.638 --> 00:11:14.340
Richard Seltzer started
as a comedian.

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:15.908
People don't know that.

00:11:15.908 --> 00:11:18.010
But I remember I saw him
in 1983

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:19.278
at Catch a Rising Star.

00:11:19.278 --> 00:11:20.879
[ Laughter ]

00:11:20.879 --> 00:11:23.382
Nice guy. Good guy.
Hated my guts.

00:11:23.382 --> 00:11:25.350
The GOP has fallen back in line
behind a guy

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:27.486
who did everything he could
to overthrow democracy

00:11:27.486 --> 00:11:29.922
and absolutely will try again,
if given the chance.

00:11:29.922 --> 00:11:31.523
A chance he, apparently,
very much wants.

00:11:31.523 --> 00:11:33.725
The details in the Senate
report are damning

00:11:33.725 --> 00:11:35.227
and there are almost
certainly more to come.

00:11:35.227 --> 00:11:36.796
There's enough material
in here --

00:11:36.796 --> 00:11:39.698
in here -- excuse me --
for ESPN --

00:11:39.698 --> 00:11:41.000
Wow, this is a real tee-up.

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:44.036
I don't know
where this is going.

00:11:44.036 --> 00:11:47.940
You guys, I never know what
the last clip's going to be.

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:50.276
That's something, you know,
we're just going to share it.

00:11:50.276 --> 00:11:52.010
You know, this is our last night
without an audience.

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:53.479
Let's just talk
to the people at home

00:11:53.479 --> 00:11:55.514
[ Laughter ]
and let them inside,

00:11:55.514 --> 00:11:58.851
behind the curtain, so to speak.

00:11:58.851 --> 00:12:00.952
There's enough material here
for ESPN

00:12:00.952 --> 00:12:03.121 line:0%
to do a four-part
"30 for 30" and call it...

00:12:03.121 --> 00:12:05.157 line:0%
-One day in January.

00:12:05.157 --> 00:12:06.225
Hm.

00:12:06.225 --> 00:12:09.728
[ Laughter ]

00:12:09.728 --> 00:12:11.163
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:11.163 --> 00:12:15.133
♪♪

